.TH CLAUDE-LCONF 1 "June 2026" "swizzle 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-lconf \- run claude with per-directory config stored under ~/.config/claude
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-lconf
.RI [ ARG " ...]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-lconf
launches
.BR claude (1)
with its
.I .claude
directory redirected from the current working directory to a mirrored path
under
.IR ~/.config/claude .
.PP
This keeps Claude configuration out of project trees and under
.IR ~/.config ,
while preserving per-directory isolation for working directories under
.IR $HOME :
each such directory gets its own subtree.
.PP
Path mapping is performed by
.BR swizzle (1)
via
.B LD_PRELOAD
so that
.B claude
itself requires no modification.
.SH PATH MAPPING
Let
.I CWD
be the current working directory.
.PP
If
.I CWD
is
.I $HOME
or a descendant of
.IR $HOME ,
the config directory is:
.PP
.RS
.I ~/.config/claude/<CWD relative to $HOME>
.RE
.PP
Otherwise the config directory is simply
.IR ~/.config/claude .
.PP
Accesses by
.B claude
to
.I CWD/.claude
(and paths beneath it) are transparently redirected to the computed config
directory.
The config directory is created if it does not already exist.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWIZZLE_BIN
Path to the
.B swizzle
binary.  Defaults to
.BR swizzle ,
but if a
.B swizzle
executable exists in the same directory as
.BR claude-lconf ,
that copy is preferred.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to derive the config directory path.
.TP
.B PWD
Used as the current working directory.  Falls back to
.BR pwd (1)
if unset.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run Claude from a project directory:
.PP
.nf
cd ~/projects/myapp
claude-lconf
.fi
.PP
Claude's config is stored in
.I ~/.config/claude/projects/myapp
instead of
.IR ~/projects/myapp/.claude .
.PP
Pass arguments through to
.BR claude :
.PP
.nf
claude-lconf --print "summarise this repo"
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.B claude-lconf
is the exit status of
.BR claude ,
or one of the exit codes documented in
.BR swizzle (1)
if setup fails before
.B claude
is reached.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swizzle (1),
.BR claude (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Barak A. Pearlmutter
